From 01944c616eff7914a7872b76d20cdaeb2cdd7902 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 04:25:30 +0000
Subject: [capra PATCH 08/11] Do not re-enter the error step after the error
 response is written

write-error-response returned nil, so tcp-handler's loop returned the
unchanged error state and stored it. Any further read on the connection
before the close took effect re-entered the same step: the response
itself is written only once, because the handled flag has already been
set, but tcp/close was queued again each time, and once the control queue
filled the resulting exception was logged for every rejected request that
had bytes left in the read buffer.

Return an inert step instead, which the loop's case does not match.
---
 src/capra/http.clj | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/capra/http.clj b/src/capra/http.clj
index 644c3c6..4604ef8 100644
--- a/src/capra/http.clj
+++ b/src/capra/http.clj
@@ -552,7 +552,7 @@
     (respond (errorf request) false)
     (when (::handler state) (close-response state nil))
     (tcp/close socket)
-    nil))
+    {::step :closed}))
 
 (defn tcp-handler
   "Create a TeensyP handler from a Ring handler."
